riginalformof", "title": {"de": "Ist das Orginal von", "en": "Is original form of", "sv": "\u00c4r originalet av"}}}, {"identifier": "https://osf.io/zhnre/files/3zk8h", "scheme": "url", "relation_type": {"id": "isidenticalto", "title": {"de": "Ist identisch mit", "en": "Is identical to", "sv": "\u00c4r identisk med"}}}, {"identifier": "https://philarchive.org/rec/VALWIB", "scheme": "url", "relation_type": {"id": "isdescribedby", "title": {"de": "Wird beschrieben von", "en": "Is described by", "sv": "Beskrivs av"}}}, {"identifier": "https://www.academia.edu/180717928/When_Interpretation_Becomes_Authority", "scheme": "url", "relation_type": {"id": "isdescribedby", "title": {"de": "Wird beschrieben von", "en": "Is described by", "sv": "Beskrivs av"}}}], "rights": [{"title": {"en": "In Copyright"}, "description": {"en": "Copyright remains with the respective rights holders. \u00a9 2026 Dorian Vale \u00b7 Museum of One. Editorial text by Dorian Vale. Alexander V. Markov\u2019s intellectual contributions are attributed throughout; rights in the original correspondence remain with its respective authors."}, "link": "https://rightsstatements.org/vocab/InC/1.0/"}], "copyright": "\u00a9 2026 Dorian Vale \u00b7 Museum of One. Editorial text by Dorian Vale. Alexander V. Markov's intellectual contributions are attributed throughout; rights in the original correspondence remain with its respective authors.", "description": "<p><strong>Full-text access.</strong> This KCWorks record preserves the unchanged nine-page, version 1.0 PDF. The canonical edition DOI is <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24130993\">10.5281/zenodo.24130993</a>; the source edition, authorship, rights and file remain unchanged.</p>\n<p>A research dialogue between Post-Interpretive Criticism and the Semiotics of Non-intentional Ephemerality.</p>\n<p>This research dialogue is Dorian Vale&rsquo;s editorial account of written correspondence with Alexander V. Markov in September and October 2026. It examines how interpretations acquire authority through their reuse in catalogues, labels, archives, teaching, and institutional procedures. Bringing Post-Interpretive Criticism into exchange with the Semiotics of Non-intentional Ephemerality, the discussion distinguishes the preservation of a text from its continuing jurisdiction, verification from warrant migration and reauthorization, and an effective correction from the maintenance of its effects. Markov&rsquo;s semantic protocol and hypothetical history of correction and lapse are considered alongside Vale&rsquo;s proposals concerning contestability, distributed responsibility, and the continuity of justificatory burden. The accompanying study, After the Interpretation Changes, supplies a separately authored documentary case concerning Simon Maris&rsquo;s Isabella; its evidence limits the stronger theoretical claims. The dialogue asks how time, place, and role affect the authority of records, and what would distinguish a changed answer from a change in the conditions governing it.</p>\n<p>The exchanges are condensed thematic paraphrases. Selection, framing, and wording are Vale&rsquo;s responsibility; this is neither a transcript nor a jointly authored statement. Disagreement and proposals not accepted by both correspondents remain explicit. Dorian Vale is the sole editorial author, affiliated with Museum of One, the publisher. Alexander V. Markov (Alexander Viktorovich Markov; \u0410\u043b\u0435\u043a\u0441\u0430\u043d\u0434\u0440 \u0412\u0438\u043a\u0442\u043e\u0440\u043e\u0432\u0438\u0447 \u041c\u0430\u0440\u043a\u043e\u0432) is the scholarly interlocutor and intellectual contributor. Institutions and artworks discussed are research subjects, not author affiliations or sponsoring organizations.</p>\n<p>Version 1.0; October 2026 edition; 9 pages; English. The edition draws on correspondence from September and October 2026 and was publicly deposited on 11 November 2026. Published in Museum of One&rsquo;s The Dialogues series and associated with the Alexander Viktorovich Markov: Critical Language and Lasting Correction research programme. Post-Interpretive Criticism and the Semiotics of Non-intentional Ephemerality remain distinct intellectual frameworks.</p>\n<p>Publisher&rsquo;s page: https://www.museumofone.art/when-interpretation-becomes-authority/<br>Research programme: https://www.museumofone.art/research-critical-language/#programme-outputs<br>Series: https://www.museumofone.art/the-dialogues/<br>Post-Interpretive Criticism: https://www.museumofone.art/doctrine/<br>Archive record MOO-CAT-022: https://archive.museumofone.art/items/24130993.html</p>\n<p><strong>Related representation.</strong> The complete corrected Research Catalogue HTML presentation, <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.22501/rc.5058205\">10.22501/rc.5058205</a>, supersedes the incomplete RC exposition 5056088. This repository presentation does not change the canonical PDF&rsquo;s DOI or version 1.0.</p>"}, "custom_fields": {"imprint:imprint": {"pages": "9"}, "kcr:edition": "Version 1.0; October 2026 edition", "kcr:project_title": "Alexander Viktorovich Markov: Critical Language and Lasting Correction", "kcr:publication_url": "https://www.museumofone.art/when-interpretation-becomes-authority/", "kcr:user_defined_tags": ["Alexander Viktorovich Markov", "\u0410\u043b\u0435\u043a\u0441\u0430\u043d\u0434\u0440 \u0412\u0438\u043a\u0442\u043e\u0440\u043e\u0432\u0438\u0447 \u041c\u0430\u0440\u043a\u043e\u0432", "Alexander V. Markov", "Dorian Vale", "Post-Interpretive Criticism", "Semiotics of Non-intentional Ephemerality", "Semantic protocol", "Successional authority", "Deactivation gap", "Recognition closure", "Interpretive authority", "Museum cataloguing", "Art criticism", "Museum studies", "Rijksmuseum", "Simon Maris", "Museum of One", "Institutional responsibility", "Contestability", "Reauthorization"], "kcr:book_series": [{"series_title": "The Dialogues"}]}, "access": {"record": "public", "files": "public", "embargo